You’re right—WLST’s Jython can choke on Pythonic shortcuts like the ternary (x if ... else y) and sometimes on with open(...). Below are WLST-safe (Jython) versions of the two scripts with those issues removed, plus a few other fixes (imports, ordering, and OSB parts made optional). These should run clean in OSB/WLS 12c WLST.

